  description={"Design internship résumé for Anh (Ace) Nguyen, a computing graduate and solo designer of the VietJusticIA mobile redesign."}
  page={"resume"}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/resume.css">
  </Fragment>
  <main class="resume-wrap" id="resume">
    <div class="resume-tools"><span>Résumé</span><a href="assets/UIUXDesignIntern_NguyenPhuocQuynhAnh.pdf" download>Download PDF</a></div>
    <article class="resume-paper" aria-label="Design internship résumé">
      <header class="resume-header">
        <h1>Nguyen Phuoc Quynh Anh</h1>
        <p class="target">UI/UX &amp; Product Design Intern</p>
        <p class="resume-contact">Son Tra, Da Nang <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="mailto:acenguyen.work@gmail.com">acenguyen.work@gmail.com</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="tel:0898543612">0898 543 612</a><br>
          <a href="index.html">Portfolio</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/npqace">linkedin.com/in/npqace</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="https://github.com/npqace">github.com/npqace</a></p>
      </header>
      <section class="resume-section">
        <h2>Profile</h2>
        <p>Computing graduate seeking a UI/UX or product design internship. I use interface audits, user flows, and wireframes to design mobile experiences and draw on hands-on web and mobile development.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="resume-section">
        <h2>Product Design</h2>
        <div class="entry"><h3><strong>VietJusticIA Mobile Redesign</strong></h3><p class="when">Solo Product Designer</p></div>
        <p>Redesigned a Vietnamese legal assistance app so readers could check a cited law and decide whether to consult a lawyer.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Audited the original app and counted four to five taps for basic tasks. Mapped user flows and wireframed bottom tabs that keep the library, assistant, lawyers, and requests within reach.</li>
          <li>Added article navigation to the document reader and surfaced specialties and consultation fees in the lawyer directory so readers could compare options before choosing a lawyer.</li>
          <li>Designed a review screen where readers can check the case brief, attached chat, citations, and fee before sending a consultation request.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="https://www.behance.net/gallery/258814687/VietJusticIA-AI-Legal-Tech-Mobile-App-Redesign">View the redesign case study on Behance</a></p>
      </section>
      <section class="resume-section">
        <h2>Technical Projects</h2>
        <div class="entry"><h3><strong>VietJusticIA Platform</strong> (University final project)</h3><p class="when">May 2025 - Dec 2025</p></div>
        <p>Built the original React Native app and React/TypeScript portal. Readers could open cited documents from chat or request a lawyer. Accepting a request in the portal opened a shared conversation with typing indicators and read receipts.</p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/npqace/vietjusticia">github.com/npqace/vietjusticia</a></p>
        <div class="entry next"><h3><strong>VSTEP Q&amp;A Bot</strong> (Club's Week)</h3><p class="when">Sep 2024</p></div>
        <p>Built a JavaScript and Flask chat that matched students' exam questions to an English or Vietnamese FAQ. Students could submit with Enter and see a typing indicator while Gemini composed a reply from the matched entry.</p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/npqace/CW-Chatbot">github.com/npqace/CW-Chatbot</a></p>
      </section>
      <section class="resume-section">
        <h2>Skills</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Design</strong>   Interface audits, information architecture, user flows, wireframes, mobile UI, reusable components.</li>
          <li><strong>Development</strong>   HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript, React, React Native, Git.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
